const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"盈利与账面价值各自提供什么",en:"What earnings and book value contribute"},body:{zh:"Ohlson把当期盈利、账面权益和股息放入同一估值框架。盈利是期间流量，账面权益是某一时点的存量，不能只凭它们和价格都有关就随意相加。模型通过明确的会计关系与未来预期，说明这几项变量为什么能够共同进入价值表达式。",en:"Ohlson connects earnings, book equity and dividends in one valuation framework. Earnings are a period flow and book equity a dated stock; their association with prices does not justify arbitrary addition. Accounting restrictions and expectations explain how they enter the same expression."},reference:{url:"https://users.metu.edu.tr/mugan/Ohlson%201995%20earnings%20bv%20div%20in%20eq%20valuation.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第664–666页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 664–666"}}},{title:{zh:"净盈余关系不是只减现金股息",en:"Clean surplus uses net distributions"},body:{zh:"期末账面权益等于期初账面权益加当期盈利，再减去净分配。这里的股息已经扣除股东投入，因此可以为负。阅读真实报表时，应先核对权益变动的范围；若有绕过损益的项目，不能默认为原模型的净盈余关系自然成立。",en:"Closing book equity equals opening book equity plus earnings less net distributions. Dividends are net of capital contributions and may be negative. Applying the relation requires reconciling the scope of equity movements; items bypassing earnings cannot simply be ignored."},reference:{url:"https://users.metu.edu.tr/mugan/Ohlson%201995%20earnings%20bv%20div%20in%20eq%20valuation.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第666页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 666"}}},{title:{zh:"剩余收益先扣期初资本占用",en:"Residual earnings charge beginning capital"},body:{zh:"异常或剩余收益，是当期盈利扣除期初账面权益所对应的资本占用成本。使用期末权益会把同一期盈利与分配混入基数。在这一语境中，“异常”指超过基准资本回报的部分，不是应计模型中的异常残差，更不是不当会计行为的同义词。",en:"Residual or abnormal earnings subtract a capital charge on beginning book equity from period earnings. Using closing equity mixes current earnings and distributions into the base. Here abnormal means above the capital-return benchmark, not an accrual-model residual or evidence of improper accounting."},reference:{url:"https://users.metu.edu.tr/mugan/Ohlson%201995%20earnings%20bv%20div%20in%20eq%20valuation.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第667页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 667"}}},{title:{zh:"账面价值加的是未来预期的现值",en:"Book value adds discounted expectations"},body:{zh:"在净盈余关系与终端条件成立时，股权价值可写为当前账面权益加未来预期剩余收益的现值。终端条件要求遥远未来的折现账面价值趋于零。这种等价转换没有消除预测任务，也不允许直接用后来实现的盈利替代当时能够形成的预期。",en:"Under clean surplus and a vanishing discounted terminal book value, equity value equals current book equity plus discounted expected residual earnings. The identity reorganizes valuation; it does not remove forecasting or permit later realized earnings to stand in for expectations available at the valuation date."},reference:{url:"https://users.metu.edu.tr/mugan/Ohlson%201995%20earnings%20bv%20div%20in%20eq%20valuation.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第667页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 667"}}},{title:{zh:"报表之外的信息并未消失",en:"Information beyond the statements remains"},body:{zh:"模型允许尚未反映在当期盈利中的其他信息影响未来剩余收益，并用特定动态方程描述其演变。该变量不是随意加入的神秘分数；它与持续性参数一起约束预测路径。若将其设为零，应明确这是一项简化，而不是证明财报已包含全部信息。",en:"Other information can affect future residual earnings before appearing in current accounting numbers. Specified dynamics and persistence parameters constrain its role. Setting that information to zero is a simplifying restriction, not evidence that financial statements already contain everything relevant."},reference:{url:"https://users.metu.edu.tr/mugan/Ohlson%201995%20earnings%20bv%20div%20in%20eq%20valuation.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第664, 668页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 664, 668"}}},{title:{zh:"理论基准与估计工作分开",en:"Separate the benchmark from estimation"},body:{zh:"这里先以风险中性、共同预期及固定利率结构建立模型，信息持续性参数也被视为已知。实际比较企业仍要处理盈利预测、资本成本、会计口径和可得时点。套入当期数字得到一个结果，并不等于这些假设已经被样本支持。",en:"The initial model uses risk neutrality, shared beliefs, a fixed interest-rate structure and known persistence parameters. Empirical comparison still needs forecasts, discount rates, consistent accounting and information dates. Substituting current figures does not validate those assumptions."},reference:{url:"https://users.metu.edu.tr/mugan/Ohlson%201995%20earnings%20bv%20div%20in%20eq%20valuation.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第664–666, 668页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 664–666, 668"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"这是在净盈余关系、折现与信息动态假设下建立的理论基准，不是由当期财报直接得出的目标价。剩余收益中的“异常”也不表示会计操纵。",en:"This is a theoretical benchmark with clean-surplus, discounting and information-dynamics assumptions, not a target price read directly from current statements. Abnormal earnings here do not mean accounting manipulation."}};export{e as default};
